ivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d198\"},\"ref\":\"d198\",\"snippet\":\" ... I watch Blacklist and The Good Doctor, and both Spader and Highmore deserve recognition.\\n\\nTotally agree on Freddie Highmore. He consistently brings outstanding performances in his role as Shaun Murphy. Every single week he nails it.\\n\\nThe Leftovers was one of the best shows ever, bar none. I ... \",\"title\":\"https://tvline.com/lists/emmys-lead-actor-drama-dream-nominations-2021/\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"41b31c6a29f5a2fce1559a1ca03b1ad29fd934041a1b4747e80d1685d5c883f2\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"173ae3cfe3364a408525829a9f42070887ee7a5af7b8e7e3dd2b22d58962e8b4\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"The Blacklist Raymond Reddington married children\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_eee5837395c64ab59e03ea27"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the clues more carefully. The \"real-life relative plays alongside but unrelated in series\" is the most distinctive. Let me think about specific shows. The combination of \"character married 3 times, only one child survives\" with a real-life relative angle is very specific. Let me reconsider \"The 100\" — the ScreenRant article mentioned Jessica and Richard Harmon (siblings) play unrelated characters. But that doesn't fit the marriage/children clues. Let me think about shows where a real-life spouse plays an unrelated character. Let me search more specifically for the \"only one child survives\" clue combined with the marriage clue.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d17\", \"start\": 3000}","name":"read"},"id":"call_b647cdd5d5364dd4bb555db4","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d17\",\"document_chars\":9101,\"end\":6000,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e2\",\"sha256\":\"296ede205a2fe113473e85be08b84f0d6833191551136843c6bff169eec542b7\",\"snapshot\":\"a531c0a6be82cbe578781b28cb207ff02e87008856d5212ec2eab3fae2afe076\",\"start\":3000,\"text\":\"ured together as a musical act. It's safe to say that the sisters' careers have been closely related to one another, and that was also true of their work on Hellcats alongside Ashley Tisdale, another former Disney Channel star.\\n\\nThe show followed Aly's character as she used her gymnastic skills to become part of a rather fiercely competitive and drama-filled cheerleading squad. The show only lasted a single season, but that gave Aly and AJ plenty of time to be on screen with one another, and kept their sisterly bond a featured aspect of both of their careers.\\n\\nJeffrey Dean Morgan And Hillarie Burton\\n\\nJeffrey Dean Morgan has made appearances in pretty much every popular television show. Currently, he's Negan, the big bad on The Walking Dead, and in that role, he's managed to call up a lot of menace from inside him. Morgan has also made appearances on the CW in Supernatural.\\n\\nOn that show, Morgan played the role of Sam and Dean Winchester's father -- the man who inspired them to begin their life hunting demons. Morgan's wife Hillarie Burton was also a regular on the CW, playing Peyton on One Tree Hill.\\n\\nThe two have never acted on the same CW show, but both were on the network at roughly the same time.\\n\\nOf course, that was long before they were married in 2014, so maybe the CW was one of the first things they talked about.\\n\\nJessica And Richard Harmon\\n\\nActors who are siblings in real life are commonly cast to play siblings on television. After all, that's the best way to make it seem like the relationship is an authentic one. In the case of Jessica and Richard Harmon, though, the siblings actually play unrelated characters in the world of The 100.\\n\\nJessica plays Niylah, a character who shows up in the third season and has been with Clarke on a couple of different occasions. Richard played John Murphy, a recurring character during the show's first two seasons who was bumped up to a major role during the third season.\\n\\nWhatever went on behind the scenes that led both of these siblings to star on the show is unclear, but it must be nice for them both to have a friendly face on set.\\n\\nJensen Ackles And Danneel Ackles\\n\\nSupernatural is one of the longest-running shows in television history, and Jensen Ackles has been one of the show's stars for its entire run. Although Ackles's co-star Jared Padalecki met his wife on the set of Supernatural, things happened a bit differently for Ackles and his wife Danneel. Jensen and Danneel started dating in 2009 and were married in 2010, but it wasn't until 2018 that Danneel showed up on Supernatural, playing a faith healer.\\n\\nInterestingly, Danneel once tweeted that if the show made it to its 13th season, which is currently airing, that would be when she decided to guest star. It turns out, that's exactly what happened.\\n\\nIn their private life, Jensen and Danneel live in Dallas, Texas with their daughter and a pair of twins.\\n\\nKatie Cassidy And Patrick Cassidy\\n\\nYou're far more likely to know Katie Cassidy than you are her\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":6000,\"ok\":true,\"previously_received\":false}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_b647cdd5d5364dd4bb555db4"},{"content":"Let me reconsider the clues more carefully. The \"real-life relative plays alongside but unrelated in series\" is the most distinctive. Let me think about specific shows. The combination of \"character married 3 times, only one child survives\" with a real-life relative angle is very specific. Let me reconsider \"The 100\" — the ScreenRant article mentioned Jessica and Richard Harmon (siblings) play unrelated characters. But that doesn't fit the marriage/children clues. Let me think about shows where a real-life spouse plays an unrelated character. Let me search more specifically for the \"only one child survives\" clue combined with the marriage clue.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"TV character married three times only one child survives series\", \"television character three marriages one surviving child\", \"TV show character widowed remarried children died one survives\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_70087f4b8378496ca95e5604","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"real life couple play unrelated characters same TV show\", \"real life siblings play unrelated characters same series\", \"married couple actors play unrelated characters television\"]}","name":"search"},"id":"call_c68abdc1efec47bdbe0076fb","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d116\"},\"ref\":\"d116\",\"snippet\":\" ... on Aidy Bryant's Hulu series Shrill and in the 2019 film James vs. His Future Self. In 2023, he joined season 4 of Apple TV+'s critically acclaimed science fiction drama For All Mankind as the character Eli Hobson.\\n\\nHe and actress Laure Mattos have been married ... \",\"title\":\"https://people.com/movies/home-alone-cast-where-are-they-now/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d36\"},\"ref\":\"d36\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 1974, the duo won their second Tony Award for their show \\\"Good Night\\\", which was the stage version of their TV series \\\"Not Only... But Also\\\".\\n\\nIn the mid- to late 1970s, they issued three comic albums in the guise of the characters \\\"Derek\\\" and \\\"Clive\\\" (Moore ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.imdb.com/search/name/?death_date=2002\"},{\"kin